  "authoringNote": "This is a missing-date vector, not an outside-interval conflict or a C01 boundary proof. The only encounter is final and usable but states encounterDate null (and no completion time), which the exact encounter body permits as \"not stated\". R04 therefore holds R04.date_not_stated with qualifier encounter.date naming that encounter, missing for the authorization coordinator, and the pair is not compared by date, so no before, after-bound or same-day condition holds; the practitioner identifiers match, so no identity condition holds. No rule reads the metadata authoredAt (2026-08-20) as a medical event date (SPEC Data contracts; guide Contracts), so it does not substitute for the missing date. R04 cites the encounter status and practitioner identifier and the order status, date and practitioner identifier (five); the null date is not cited. A missing finding names no parent (C07). The order states its date and the receipt follows its span (C06), so R05 passes. R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_information.",
